If you don't understand pointers and are modifying NetHack's source,
you're just asking for trouble:-) It'd be really OT to discuss them
here, but I think the best thing you can do anyway is get some text on C
and learn it a bit (or perhaps not only a bit--it's not such a big
language after all), on yourself. What I mean is that NetHack might be a
pleasant program to practice on, but you won't get away without knowing
the basics of the language it's programmed on--it's too complex for that.

