Try compiling the official source with -DDEBUG first. Do you still get
errors?

> NetHack's DEBUG messages don't help me very much. They only seem to 
> give out stuff concerning stat or hunger checks, as well as the 
> mkportal message that I had already included because of my specific
> problem with portals. It was because of this (DEBUG didn't help) that
> I decided on tackling gdb - with zero success up to now!

After you learn how C implements functions, handles pointers, etc.,
you'll be also able to read the instructions on gdb easily. The basics
are: compile with debugging info (-g), set breakpoints (br), watchpoints
(wa), backtrace (bt), and run in wizard mode (r -D) to ease debugging.
Take care to run gdb on the binary, and not on the starting script.

